        "original_id": "1afbc7cb-8679-5fcd-8966-3f7959088f01",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: George Harrison, Paul McCartney, the Beatles\n- Albums: Come and Get It: The Best of Apple Records\n- Concepts: record production, Hinduism, Indian instrumentation\n\nFacts:\n- George Harrison was often referred to as \"the quiet Beatle.\"\n- George Harrison embraced Hinduism and influenced his fellow Beatles and their American audience by incorporating Indian instrumentation into the Beatles' music.\n- In most cases, the recordings on the album Come and Get It: The Best of Apple Records were produced by one of the Beatles.\n- George Harrison and Paul McCartney were the most heavily represented Beatles producers on the album Come and Get It: The Best of Apple Records.",
